    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0728" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">310.2/9–853: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Aldrich</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-09-08T12:00:00+01:00">September 8,
                            1953—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>993. Department pass USUN 10; Deptel 1235, September 5. Foreign Office
                    hesitates concur Secretary’s suggestion re Chinese representation UN, pointing out new GA ruling has never been tested. If, for example, GA did fix December closing date, there would be
                    nothing prevent GA on closing date issue new
                    ruling it would merely adjourn and resume after Christmas recess. If, on other
                    hand, Foreign Office could be assured firm closing date December, it would go
                        along.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d463-f1"/></p>
                <p>Foreign Office plans telegraph USUN in above
                    sense this afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aldrich</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d463-f1" n="1" xml:id="d463-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal notation by the Director of the Office of UN Political and Security Affairs (Wainhouse), with reference to the words
                    “be assured firm closing date December, it would go along”, in the last sentence
                    of this paragraph: “We will do our best &amp; with UK support we are reasonably certain to prevail. We can’t give
                    guarantees on this however. D[avid]
                        W[ainhouse]”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
